{
  "iri": "https://strandz.it/jigdaw/plugins/sprout/",
  "label": "Sprout",
  "comment": "L-system MIDI generator: a grammar is rewritten for up to 16 generations, read as a turtle, and played as a monophonic, scale-quantised line locked to the host transport, optionally growing by one generation every few bars.",
  "vendor": "danja",
  "developer": "http://danny.ayers.name",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "format": "trn:Jig , trn:WebAudio",
  "licenceId": "MIT",
  "prefers": [],
  "registeredName": "sprout",
  "roles": [
    "trn:MidiGenerator"
  ],
  "accepts": [
    "trn:Midi",
    "trn:ControlMidi"
  ],
  "produces": [
    "trn:Midi"
  ],
  "cautions": [
    "Silent until the host transport is rolling and reports a tempo and a beat position. Pure MIDI, no audio: route its MIDI output to an instrument. Ported from the Downspout VST3 of the same name; the status read-outs and the panel are not carried over, and the random draw differs, so a seed gives a different line from the VST3's.",
    "Monophonic by design. A new note ends the note before it rather than overlapping. An expansion longer than 131,072 symbols is not used; the deepest generation that fits plays instead.",
    "Declares no jig:module and so no jig:abi. A host that loads a module directly, such as the native adapter, cannot load this plugin; a JavaScript AudioWorklet host can."
  ],
  "requires": [
    "jig:MidiEvents",
    "jig:MidiOut",
    "trn:HostTransport"
  ],
  "shape": {
    "stateless": true,
    "audioInputs": 0,
    "audioOutputs": 0,
    "renderQuantum": 128,
    "latencyFrames": 0
  },
  "resources": {
    "processor": "sprout-processor.js"
  },
